After some trial an error, I have narrowed the issue down to two PSMs from the same run in the input. If they are both included, the data processing fails, if either are filtered out first, the data processes successfully.<br><div>I&#39;ve attached a .csv of the two PSMs causing trouble.</div><div>I also suspect that the problem may be occurring sooner, as I hadn&#39;t noticed that there were suppressed warnings from the `MSstatsPTM::PDtoMSstatsPTMFormat` call. The warning messages are &quot;
<span aria-label="Console Output" role="document"><span role="document"><span>In `[.data.table`(input_duplicates, , `:=`(keep, .summarizeMultiplePSMs(.SD,  ... :
  Coercing &#39;character&#39; RHS to &#39;logical&#39; to match the type of target vector.</span></span></span>&quot;</div><div><br></div><div>For now my solution is to manually remove one of the PSMs before pre-processing for input.</div><div><br></div><div>Sam</div>
